# How to cite OpenKeito (Citation File Format, https://citation-file-format.github.io).
#
# RELEASE: `version` and `date-released` are set at every release (AGENTS.md,
# "Versions and releases"); the values below are those of the last release.
# The authors are named as in LICENSE-MIT until the maintainers decide otherwise.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "OpenKeito"
abstract: >-
  An open electromagnetic transient (EMT) simulator for power systems, driven by
  people and AI agents: models as JSON documents, a solver verified against
  closed-form solutions, conversion from pandapower and PowSyBl (CGMES) networks
  that starts from their power flow, schedules, and an MCP server.
authors:
  - name: "The OpenKeito contributors"
version: "0.16.0"
date-released: "2026-11-28"
license:
  - MIT
  - Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/yutanakamurajp/OpenKeito"
keywords:
  - power systems
  - electromagnetic transients
  - EMT
  - simulation
